	<key>readme</key>
	<string># VS Code Project Switcher

Type `proj` and a few characters of a project name; press Return to open that
project in VS Code. If the project is already open, its existing window is
focused instead (VS Code never opens the same folder twice).

- ⏎ — open or focus the project
- ⌘⏎ — force a new window
- ⌥⏎ — reveal the folder in Finder
- ⇥ — autocomplete the selected project name

Projects are found by walking the Projects Root: any folder with a `.git` is
a project, other folders are groupings to look inside, and plain org/project
folders (e.g. `~/Code/gascity/gas-city-inc`) count too. Configure the root in
this workflow's configuration sheet.</string>
